## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about cross-tenant data isolation, token binding, and incident response in a realistic multi-tenant platform similar to large-scale chat/workspace products.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege per-automation scopes
- Token binding to tenant identity and audience (aud/iss)
- Short-lived tokens with rapid rotation
- Per-resource RBAC/ACL enforcement
- API gateway policy checks and runtime validation
- Tamper-evident audit logs and a 24h IR playbook

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation: verify JWT claims for a request
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authorize(token, requiredScope, tenantId) {
  const payload = jwt.verify(token, PUBLIC_KEY, { algorithms:['RS256'] });
  if (payload.aud !== 'automation') return false;
  if (payload.tenant !== tenantId) return false;
  if (!payload.scopes.includes(requiredScope)) return false;
  // ensure token is recent
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design token rotation and revocation in case of breach?
- What telemetry would you collect to detect automation token abuse?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design defense-in-depth security controls in a Kubernetes multi-tenant fintech environment, focusing on namespace isolation, secure image supply chains, and incident response readiness.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes RBAC and namespace isolation
- Container image signing (cosign/Sigstore) and SBOMs
- Policy enforcement with OPA/Gatekeeper
- Service mesh mTLS and network policies
- CI/CD pipeline security checks for secrets
- Incident response with credential rotation and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: verify signed image (pseudo-code)
const cosign = require('@sigstore/cosign');

async function verifyImage(imageRef, publicKey) {
  try {
    const verification = await cosign.verify(imageRef, { publicKey });
    if (!verification.verified) {
      throw new Error('Image signature verification failed');
    }
    return verification;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Verification error:', error);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

## Implementation Considerations

- Implement tiered access controls with least privilege principles
- Establish automated policy enforcement at multiple layers
- Create comprehensive monitoring and alerting for policy violations
- Develop regular security testing and validation procedures
